{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VX7RJwoqXZJ5H7nWVtkrJn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"PLAN-135 W2 H1 (ADR-153 compaction-continuity) — PreCompact governance\n3\tsnapshot.\n4\t\n5\tCompaction is the OTHER way a session's protocol state dies — the\n6\tcloseout-guard (S228) covers only Stop. When the Claude Code harness fires\n7\t``PreCompact`` (manual ``/compact`` or auto context-window threshold), this\n8\thook snapshots, into the plan-scoped scratchpad, the governance state the\n9\tpost-compaction transcript would otherwise forget:\n10\t\n11\t  - ``plan_id`` — the PLAN-NNN currently scoped to the session (derived from\n12\t    the audit-log ``plan_transition`` events, NOT an env var — agent-spoofable;\n13\t    scratchpad_lib.resolve_plan_id doctrine);\n14\t  - ``execution_unit`` — the active execution-unit position (the first\n15\t    unchecked ``- [ ]`` checkbox in the current plan file, repo-relative path\n16\t    + line + sanitized label);\n17\t  - ``ceremony_flags`` — pending Owner-GPG ceremony breadcrumbs (executable\n18\t    ``finish-*.sh`` under ``staged/**`` / ``scripts/local/`` newer than the\n19\t    last git tag — the closeout-guard's signal, reused);\n20\t  - ``hmac_chain`` — a READ-ONLY breadcrumb of the audit HMAC-chain state\n21\t    (last-hmac hex PREFIX + chain-length counter) so a post-compaction\n22\t    integrity check has the pre-compaction anchor.\n23\t\n24\tThe matching ``PostCompact`` hook (``check_postcompact_reinject.py``) reads\n25\tthis snapshot back and reinjects governance POINTERS (not the snapshot body)\n26\tvia ``additionalContext``.\n27\t\n28\t## PLAN-179 W1 US3 — session-scope fallback (the ADR-153 fires-proof cure)\n29\t\n30\tThe S309 fires-proof was NEGATIVE for the dominant path: ``resolve_plan_id``\n31\tneeds a ``plan_transition`` event *from this same session*, and a real session\n32\temits ~0 of those (2 events in 12.515 log lines), so every long session — the\n33\tonly kind that ever compacts — snapshotted NOTHING. The write is no longer\n34\tskipped when the plan is unresolved: it goes to a SESSION-scoped store\n35\t(``scratchpad_lib.open_session_scratchpad``) and reports the new outcome\n36\t``written_session_scope``. Per emenda r1-C1 the session id comes ONLY from the\n37\thook input — if the derivation would fall back to ``CLAUDE_SESSION_ID`` (env,\n38\tagent-spoofable — consensus M2) the fallback is REFUSED and the outcome stays\n39\t``scratchpad_unavailable``; the scope is recorded in the blob's own\n40\t``scope_kind`` field, never by overloading ``plan_id`` (the store's\n41\tplan-isolation invariant stays intact).\n42\t\n43\t## Contract\n44\t\n45\t- ADVISORY + fail-open (PLAN-091 S116 doctrine: parse errors / missing files /\n46\t  derivation failures / timeouts → stderr breadcrumb + emit ``{}``). NEVER\n47\t  blocks — a crashed snapshot must not stop a compaction.\n48\t- Time budget ``TIME_BUDGET_S`` (subprocess git capped; budget-blown → snapshot\n49\t  what we have, never noise).\n50\t- Emits ONE closed-enum ``compaction_continuity_snapshot`` audit event\n51\t  (registered in BOTH ``_KNOWN_ACTIONS`` and SPEC v2.43) carrying ONLY closed\n52\t  enums + counters: ``trigger`` (manual/auto/other), ``snapshot_outcome``\n53\t  (written/written_session_scope/scratchpad_unavailable/error/other),\n54\t  ``plan_id`` (PLAN-NNN or ``unknown``), ``chain_length`` (clamped int). The\n55\t  snapshot BODY (plan path text, checkbox label, ceremony paths, last-hmac\n56\t  hex) is written to the scratchpad — NEVER to the audit wire.\n57\t- Snapshot privacy: the write is plan- or session-scoped and secrets-redacted\n58\t  by ``state_store.set``; the audit emit carries no path/label text.\n59\t  **PLAN-179 amendment 8.3 (debate C9):** this claim used to be FALSE on the\n60\t  path actually taken — ``state_store.set`` redacts ``isinstance(value, str)``\n61\t  ONLY and this hook handed it ``payload.encode(\"utf-8\")``, i.e. bytes, which\n62\t  the store trusts verbatim. The snapshot is now passed as a ``str`` so the\n63\t  store's own redactor runs. Same rule for the session-scoped write.\n64\t- Kill-switch: ``CEO_COMPACTION_CONTINUITY=0`` (shared with the PostCompact\n65\t  reinjection half). It also disables the session-store GC below — the switch\n66\t  turns the whole feature off, housekeeping included.\n67\t- PLAN-179 rail finding C: this hook is the PRODUCTION CALLER of\n68\t  ``scratchpad_lib.gc_orphan_session_stores`` (see ``_gc_session_stores``).\n69\t  The session-scope fallback creates one sqlite store per unresolved-plan\n70\t  session and row-TTL expiry cannot unlink a FILE, so without a caller the\n71\t  fallback accumulated files without bound. The sweep runs last, is bounded by\n72\t  the library's own per-run cap, respects the remaining time budget and is\n73\t  fail-open: no snapshot outcome depends on it.\n74\t- PLAN-179 W0 US2b progress guard: OBSERVE + NOTIFY only (see\n75\t  ``_progress_guard``); it emits ``context_pressure_observed`` and a stderr\n76\t  breadcrumb, and is DISABLED unless ``CEO_CONTEXT_PROGRESS_FLOOR_TOKENS`` is\n77\t  set. It cannot halt a compaction — PreCompact has no deny channel.\n78\t- Stdlib only, Python >= 3.9.\n79\t\n80\t## Scratchpad key\n81\t\n82\t``compaction_continuity`` (single JSON blob, <64 KiB; ``set`` overwrites). The\n83\tPostCompact half reads this exact key — in the plan scope first, then (PLAN-179\n84\tW1 US3) in the session scope.\n85\t\"\"\"\n86\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n87\t\n88\timport contextlib\n89\timport fnmatch\n90\timport glob\n91\timport json\n92\timport os\n93\timport re\n94\timport stat as stat_mod\n95\timport subprocess\n96\timport sys\n97\timport time\n98\tfrom typing import Any, Dict, Iterator, List, Optional, Tuple\n99\t\n100\t# Make the local `_lib` importable (matches the pattern of existing hooks).\n101\tfrom pathlib import Path\n102\t\n103\t_HOOKS_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n104\tif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n105\t    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\n106\t\n107\tTIME_BUDGET_S = 2.5\n108\tSCRATCHPAD_KEY = \"compaction_continuity\"\n109\tMAX_CEREMONY_FLAGS = 5\n110\t# Snapshot blob is capped well under the scratchpad 64 KiB per-key limit; the\n111\t# label/path clamps below keep it small regardless.\n112\t_LABEL_CLAMP = 160\n113\t_PATH_CLAMP = 200\n114\t\n115\t# PLAN-179 W1 US3 / emenda r1-C2 — the session-scoped store is created per\n116\t# session id, so it accumulates files the plan-scoped one does not. Every\n117\t# session-scope write carries an EXPLICIT ttl so an orphaned snapshot expires\n118\t# on its own even before the file-level GC item ships. Hygiene value (7 days),\n119\t# not a decision-bearing number.\n120\tSESSION_SNAPSHOT_TTL_S = 7 * 24 * 3600\n121\t\n122\t# PLAN-179 W0 US2b — progress-guard floor. The plan's own words: \"requer o `F`\n123\t# medido acima; até lá o piso não tem valor honesto\". So there is NO default\n124\t# here: absent/malformed env => the guard is a NO-OP. Once W0 measures F and T\n125\t# the operator sets the env var; a literal default would be a magic number\n126\t# shipped ahead of its measurement.\n127\tPROGRESS_FLOOR_ENV = \"CEO_CONTEXT_PROGRESS_FLOOR_TOKENS\"\n128\t\n129\t# PLAN-179 W0 US2b / amendment 8.1 — WIRE CONTRACT for `context_pressure_observed`.\n130\t#\n131\t# INTEGRATION DEFECT CLOSED HERE (PLAN-179 W0/W1 cross-file pass): this hook\n132\t# used to compute a TOKEN-COUNT bucket (`used_tokens // 10000`, clamped 999)\n133\t# and emit it as `used_tokens_bucket=` alongside `floor_tokens=`. Neither field\n134\t# name exists in `_lib/audit_emit._CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST`, whose\n135\t# scrub is DENY-BY-DEFAULT — so both were dropped and every emit landed as a\n136\t# bare `used_bucket=0`. The wire field is `used_bucket` and it is a COARSE\n137\t# INTEGER PERCENT rung (share of the context window consumed), never a raw or\n138\t# token-derived count: a raw count is a transcript-size side channel, and a\n139\t# FLOAT under the HMAC chain discards the WHOLE event\n140\t# ([[feedback-float-in-hmac-field-drops-whole-event]]).\n141\t#\n142\t# The rung SET is DERIVED from audit_emit at call time, never restated here\n143\t# ([[feedback-closed-sets-must-be-derived-not-recalled]]): a literal copy would\n144\t# drift from the scrub branch that validates it and the event would coerce to\n145\t# the 0 sentinel forever, i.e. exactly the silent dead instrument this pass\n146\t# exists to remove.\n147\t_PRESSURE_RUNGS_ATTR = \"_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_USED_BUCKETS_PCT\"\n148\t# This producer's value inside audit_emit._CONTEXT_PRESSURE_EVENT_SOURCES.\n149\t_PRESSURE_EVENT_SOURCE = \"precompact\"\n150\t# audit_emit's documented \"unrecognized / absent bucket\" sentinel — deliberately\n151\t# OUTSIDE the percent enum so a consumer can always tell a real rung from a\n152\t# coerced one. Emitted when the hook input carries no context-window accounting.\n153\t_PRESSURE_BUCKET_UNKNOWN = 0\n154\t# `should_emit_context_pressure(used_bucket, state_dir)` keeps its edge-trigger\n155\t# marker under `<project>/.claude/state` (its own docstring names that path).\n156\t_PRESSURE_STATE_SUBPATH = (\".claude\", \"state\")\n157\t\n158\t# Candidate shapes for the harness's context-window accounting. These MIRROR\n159\t# `.claude/scripts/statusline-ceo.py:context_pct()` — the one place in this repo\n160\t# that already reverse-engineered the harness payload — rather than being\n161\t# guessed here. Absent ⇒ no percent is invented\n162\t# ([[feedback-measurement-must-list-its-inputs]]).\n163\t_CONTEXT_WINDOW_KEYS = (\"context_window\", \"context\", \"context_usage\")\n164\t_CONTEXT_PCT_KEYS = (\"used_percentage\", \"used_pct\", \"percent_used\")\n165\t_CONTEXT_USED_KEYS = (\"used_tokens\", \"input_tokens\", \"total_input_tokens\")\n166\t_CONTEXT_SIZE_KEYS = (\"context_window_size\", \"max_tokens\", \"size\")\n167\t\n168\t# The implementation is split into installable hooks/_lib modules. Loading the\n169\t# real source files into this facade preserves private names, global state and\n170\t# monkeypatch seams from the historical hook. Compatibility markers remain\n171\t# here for staged source selectors: written_session_scope, _sidecar_override_safe.\n172\tfrom _lib._precompact_parts import install as _install_precompact_parts  # noqa: E402\n173\t\n174\t_install_precompact_parts(globals())\n175\tdel _install_precompact_parts\n176\t\n177\t\n178\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n179\t    main()\n180\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"506ec16a-dc13-438e-b350-67d3c029ffa9","uuid":"7adf485b-984c-4a4d-94b0-62556e540b32","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:55:05.579Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/check_precompact_continuity.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"PLAN-135 W2 H1 (ADR-153 compaction-continuity) — PreCompact governance\nsnapshot.\n\nCompaction is the OTHER way a session's protocol state dies — the\ncloseout-guard (S228) covers only Stop. When the Claude Code harness fires\n``PreCompact`` (manual ``/compact`` or auto context-window threshold), this\nhook snapshots, into the plan-scoped scratchpad, the governance state the\npost-compaction transcript would otherwise forget:\n\n  - ``plan_id`` — the PLAN-NNN currently scoped to the session (derived from\n    the audit-log ``plan_transition`` events, NOT an env var — agent-spoofable;\n    scratchpad_lib.resolve_plan_id doctrine);\n  - ``execution_unit`` — the active execution-unit position (the first\n    unchecked ``- [ ]`` checkbox in the current plan file, repo-relative path\n    + line + sanitized label);\n  - ``ceremony_flags`` — pending Owner-GPG ceremony breadcrumbs (executable\n    ``finish-*.sh`` under ``staged/**`` / ``scripts/local/`` newer than the\n    last git tag — the closeout-guard's signal, reused);\n  - ``hmac_chain`` — a READ-ONLY breadcrumb of the audit HMAC-chain state\n    (last-hmac hex PREFIX + chain-length counter) so a post-compaction\n    integrity check has the pre-compaction anchor.\n\nThe matching ``PostCompact`` hook (``check_postcompact_reinject.py``) reads\nthis snapshot back and reinjects governance POINTERS (not the snapshot body)\nvia ``additionalContext``.\n\n## PLAN-179 W1 US3 — session-scope fallback (the ADR-153 fires-proof cure)\n\nThe S309 fires-proof was NEGATIVE for the dominant path: ``resolve_plan_id``\nneeds a ``plan_transition`` event *from this same session*, and a real session\nemits ~0 of those (2 events in 12.515 log lines), so every long session — the\nonly kind that ever compacts — snapshotted NOTHING. The write is no longer\nskipped when the plan is unresolved: it goes to a SESSION-scoped store\n(``scratchpad_lib.open_session_scratchpad``) and reports the new outcome\n``written_session_scope``. Per emenda r1-C1 the session id comes ONLY from the\nhook input — if the derivation would fall back to ``CLAUDE_SESSION_ID`` (env,\nagent-spoofable — consensus M2) the fallback is REFUSED and the outcome stays\n``scratchpad_unavailable``; the scope is recorded in the blob's own\n``scope_kind`` field, never by overloading ``plan_id`` (the store's\nplan-isolation invariant stays intact).\n\n## Contract\n\n- ADVISORY + fail-open (PLAN-091 S116 doctrine: parse errors / missing files /\n  derivation failures / timeouts → stderr breadcrumb + emit ``{}``). NEVER\n  blocks — a crashed snapshot must not stop a compaction.\n- Time budget ``TIME_BUDGET_S`` (subprocess git capped; budget-blown → snapshot\n  what we have, never noise).\n- Emits ONE closed-enum ``compaction_continuity_snapshot`` audit event\n  (registered in BOTH ``_KNOWN_ACTIONS`` and SPEC v2.43) carrying ONLY closed\n  enums + counters: ``trigger`` (manual/auto/other), ``snapshot_outcome``\n  (written/written_session_scope/scratchpad_unavailable/error/other),\n  ``plan_id`` (PLAN-NNN or ``unknown``), ``chain_length`` (clamped int). The\n  snapshot BODY (plan path text, checkbox label, ceremony paths, last-hmac\n  hex) is written to the scratchpad — NEVER to the audit wire.\n- Snapshot privacy: the write is plan- or session-scoped and secrets-redacted\n  by ``state_store.set``; the audit emit carries no path/label text.\n  **PLAN-179 amendment 8.3 (debate C9):** this claim used to be FALSE on the\n  path actually taken — ``state_store.set`` redacts ``isinstance(value, str)``\n  ONLY and this hook handed it ``payload.encode(\"utf-8\")``, i.e. bytes, which\n  the store trusts verbatim. The snapshot is now passed as a ``str`` so the\n  store's own redactor runs. Same rule for the session-scoped write.\n- Kill-switch: ``CEO_COMPACTION_CONTINUITY=0`` (shared with the PostCompact\n  reinjection half). It also disables the session-store GC below — the switch\n  turns the whole feature off, housekeeping included.\n- PLAN-179 rail finding C: this hook is the PRODUCTION CALLER of\n  ``scratchpad_lib.gc_orphan_session_stores`` (see ``_gc_session_stores``).\n  The session-scope fallback creates one sqlite store per unresolved-plan\n  session and row-TTL expiry cannot unlink a FILE, so without a caller the\n  fallback accumulated files without bound. The sweep runs last, is bounded by\n  the library's own per-run cap, respects the remaining time budget and is\n  fail-open: no snapshot outcome depends on it.\n- PLAN-179 W0 US2b progress guard: OBSERVE + NOTIFY only (see\n  ``_progress_guard``); it emits ``context_pressure_observed`` and a stderr\n  breadcrumb, and is DISABLED unless ``CEO_CONTEXT_PROGRESS_FLOOR_TOKENS`` is\n  set. It cannot halt a compaction — PreCompact has no deny channel.\n- Stdlib only, Python >= 3.9.\n\n## Scratchpad key\n\n``compaction_continuity`` (single JSON blob, <64 KiB; ``set`` overwrites). The\nPostCompact half reads this exact key — in the plan scope first, then (PLAN-179\nW1 US3) in the session scope.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport contextlib\nimport fnmatch\nimport glob\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport stat as stat_mod\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Iterator, List, Optional, Tuple\n\n# Make the local `_lib` importable (matches the pattern of existing hooks).\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n_HOOKS_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\n\nTIME_BUDGET_S = 2.5\nSCRATCHPAD_KEY = \"compaction_continuity\"\nMAX_CEREMONY_FLAGS = 5\n# Snapshot blob is capped well under the scratchpad 64 KiB per-key limit; the\n# label/path clamps below keep it small regardless.\n_LABEL_CLAMP = 160\n_PATH_CLAMP = 200\n\n# PLAN-179 W1 US3 / emenda r1-C2 — the session-scoped store is created per\n# session id, so it accumulates files the plan-scoped one does not. Every\n# session-scope write carries an EXPLICIT ttl so an orphaned snapshot expires\n# on its own even before the file-level GC item ships. Hygiene value (7 days),\n# not a decision-bearing number.\nSESSION_SNAPSHOT_TTL_S = 7 * 24 * 3600\n\n# PLAN-179 W0 US2b — progress-guard floor. The plan's own words: \"requer o `F`\n# medido acima; até lá o piso não tem valor honesto\". So there is NO default\n# here: absent/malformed env => the guard is a NO-OP. Once W0 measures F and T\n# the operator sets the env var; a literal default would be a magic number\n# shipped ahead of its measurement.\nPROGRESS_FLOOR_ENV = \"CEO_CONTEXT_PROGRESS_FLOOR_TOKENS\"\n\n# PLAN-179 W0 US2b / amendment 8.1 — WIRE CONTRACT for `context_pressure_observed`.\n#\n# INTEGRATION DEFECT CLOSED HERE (PLAN-179 W0/W1 cross-file pass): this hook\n# used to compute a TOKEN-COUNT bucket (`used_tokens // 10000`, clamped 999)\n# and emit it as `used_tokens_bucket=` alongside `floor_tokens=`. Neither field\n# name exists in `_lib/audit_emit._CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST`, whose\n# scrub is DENY-BY-DEFAULT — so both were dropped and every emit landed as a\n# bare `used_bucket=0`. The wire field is `used_bucket` and it is a COARSE\n# INTEGER PERCENT rung (share of the context window consumed), never a raw or\n# token-derived count: a raw count is a transcript-size side channel, and a\n# FLOAT under the HMAC chain discards the WHOLE event\n# ([[feedback-float-in-hmac-field-drops-whole-event]]).\n#\n# The rung SET is DERIVED from audit_emit at call time, never restated here\n# ([[feedback-closed-sets-must-be-derived-not-recalled]]): a literal copy would\n# drift from the scrub branch that validates it and the event would coerce to\n# the 0 sentinel forever, i.e. exactly the silent dead instrument this pass\n# exists to remove.\n_PRESSURE_RUNGS_ATTR = \"_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_USED_BUCKETS_PCT\"\n# This producer's value inside audit_emit._CONTEXT_PRESSURE_EVENT_SOURCES.\n_PRESSURE_EVENT_SOURCE = \"precompact\"\n# audit_emit's documented \"unrecognized / absent bucket\" sentinel — deliberately\n# OUTSIDE the percent enum so a consumer can always tell a real rung from a\n# coerced one. Emitted when the hook input carries no context-window accounting.\n_PRESSURE_BUCKET_UNKNOWN = 0\n# `should_emit_context_pressure(used_bucket, state_dir)` keeps its edge-trigger\n# marker under `<project>/.claude/state` (its own docstring names that path).\n_PRESSURE_STATE_SUBPATH = (\".claude\", \"state\")\n\n# Candidate shapes for the harness's context-window accounting. These MIRROR\n# `.claude/scripts/statusline-ceo.py:context_pct()` — the one place in this repo\n# that already reverse-engineered the harness payload — rather than being\n# guessed here. Absent ⇒ no percent is invented\n# ([[feedback-measurement-must-list-its-inputs]]).\n_CONTEXT_WINDOW_KEYS = (\"context_window\", \"context\", \"context_usage\")\n_CONTEXT_PCT_KEYS = (\"used_percentage\", \"used_pct\", \"percent_used\")\n_CONTEXT_USED_KEYS = (\"used_tokens\", \"input_tokens\", \"total_input_tokens\")\n_CONTEXT_SIZE_KEYS = (\"context_window_size\", \"max_tokens\", \"size\")\n\n# The implementation is split into installable hooks/_lib modules. Loading the\n# real source files into this facade preserves private names, global state and\n# monkeypatch seams from the historical hook. Compatibility markers remain\n# here for staged source selectors: written_session_scope, _sidecar_override_safe.\nfrom _lib._precompact_parts import install as _install_precompact_parts  # noqa: E402\n\n_install_precompact_parts(globals())\ndel _install_precompact_parts\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","numLines":180,"startLine":1,"totalLines":180}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VX7RJwoqXZJ5H7nWVtkrJn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
